{"text": "2026-03-27 15:44:26.447 | INFO     | trpg_py.agent.planner:_run_evidence_stage:629 - planner evidence_agent stage started\n", "record": {"elapsed": {"repr": "0:00:01.026046", "seconds": 1.026046}, "exception": null, "extra": {"planner_run_id": "78055490b730", "planner_thread_id": "6ad7eab79aac4f4988171399e4989b77", "planner_round": "evidence_agent", "planner_input_mode": "prompt", "planner_event": "evidence_stage_start", "planner_input_snapshot": {"messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Stage: evidence_agent.\nYour job in this stage is to gather evidence only.\nDo not draft or repair a TaskDocument in this stage.\nUse only search, list, and read to collect enough information for the DSL stage.\nReturn status ready with an evidence_bundle when the evidence is sufficient for dsl_agent.\nReturn status needs_human with concrete questions when more human input is required.\nReturn status blocked only for genuine system failures.\n\nEvidenceBundle must be lightweight and include:\n- summary\n- facts[] with name, value_summary, source_paths, source_kind, optional note\n- missing_info\n- assumptions\n- ready_for_dsl\n\nPlan the DM instruction into a TaskDocument for the TRPG engine.\n\nA valid TaskDocument is an execution DSL. It is not a natural-language plan.\n\nTaskDocument minimal shape:\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"string\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"policy\": {},\n  \"context\": {},\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"string\",\n      \"type\": \"select|check|damage|heal|resource|effect|state\",\n      \"kind\": \"depends on type\",\n      \"args\": {},\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"when\": null\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nAllowed type/kind pairs:\n- select: target | area | filtered\n- check: attack | save | ability | skill\n- damage: apply\n- heal: apply\n- resource: consume\n- effect: add | remove\n- state: set | adjust\n\nReference rules:\n- Use {\"$ref\": \"context.foo\"}, {\"$ref\": \"state.actors.hero_1.ac\"}, or {\"$ref\": \"result.attack_roll.outcome\"}.\n- A step may only reference results from earlier steps.\n- Use \"when\" for conditional execution.\n\nPath semantics:\n- list and read use bare store paths such as actors.goblin_1.ac, actors.aldera.hp, or actors.goblin_1.attacks.scimitar.to_hit.\n- Do not pass state.actors.goblin_1.ac directly to list or read.\n- TaskDocument $ref values keep engine namespaces, so the matching reference form is state.actors.goblin_1.ac.\n- Think of this as: tool path actors.goblin_1.ac -> TaskDocument $ref state.actors.goblin_1.ac.\n\nTool responsibilities:\n- Use search for rule evidence.\n- Use list to discover...<truncated>"}]}}, "file": {"name": "planner.py", "path": "/home/naifen/code/trpg-py/trpg_py/agent/planner.py"}, "function": "_run_evidence_stage", "level": {"icon": "ℹ️", "name": "INFO", "no": 20}, "line": 629, "message": "planner evidence_agent stage started", "module": "planner", "name": "trpg_py.agent.planner", "process": {"id": 94992, "name": "MainProcess"}, "thread": {"id": 126846201681728, "name": "MainThread"}, "time": {"repr": "2026-03-27 15:44:26.447513+08:00", "timestamp": 1774597466.447513}}}
